To make a button display:none in HTML and CSS while keeping the image inside of it visible, you can use the following steps:

1. First, add the image inside the button element in HTML. For example:

```
<button class="hidden">
   <img src="image.jpg">
</button>
```

2. Apply a specific class to the button element, such as "hidden", that will hide it using CSS. You can use the following code:

```
.hidden {
   display: none;
}
```

This will hide the entire button element, including any contents inside it.

3. To keep the image inside the hidden button visible, you can apply CSS styles to the image using a separate selector. For example:

```
.hidden img {
   visibility: visible;
}
```

This will make the image inside the hidden button visible while the button element itself remains hidden. You can adjust the style of the image to suit your needs, such as setting its position, size, or opacity.

Note that setting visibility: visible on the image will only make the image visible, not clickable. If you need the image to be clickable in place of the hidden button, you can add a JavaScript event listener to the image that performs the same action as the button click.

